@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what the choice prompt draws, what may be offered, and where the cursor may rest
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui_test.go, internal/choiceui/screen_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/hover_test.go, internal/choiceui/gated_reason_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/pane_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go, internal/run/params.go, internal/run/run_test.go
' covers: internal/run/run_form_order_test.go
' Destination diagram — prose from internal/choiceui/choiceui.go and cmd/proveo/main.go's
' row-gating helpers (applicableRows, comingSoon, gateAddons; gateReview went with
' the review tier) lands here (batches 3 and 6).
' consent.go (Consent, the review tier's connection modal) and its test are
' DELETED (MEASURED): review was retired 2026-10-16 and nothing called it.
' drawBorder moved to internal/choiceui/blocked_run.go, where the blocked-run
' prompts used it; the `rendered` test helper lives in screen_test.go since
' the Bubble Tea port (_spec/internal/choiceui/tui-stack.puml).
' What the answers MEAN and how they are cached: _spec/internal/agentsettings/choice-cache.puml.
' Resolved geometry — column alignment, the divider, how a gated element is drawn:
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (salt). Layout prose belongs there, not here.
' Why a full-screen prompt needs proveo to own the pty:
' _spec/internal/ptyproxy/pty-ownership.puml. (The review gate that first forced
' it was retired 2026-09-16 with the docker egress mechanism.)
' Why the sandbox box is compulsory and what the escape is:
' _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml.
' The topology strip drawn under the help block: _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHY HELP EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS KEYED ───────────────────────────────────
' ── A GREYED BOX THAT STATES A FACT, AND WHY IT KEEPS ITS STATE ────────────
' addonFixed are the boxes that state a FACT rather than offer a choice: their
' state is never the operator's to change, and drawing them is how the plane
' says what it EXCLUDES. "host" is the alternative an operator might otherwise
' assume unticking the daemon selects — it never is, because proveo
' containerises every run — and the TUI is the interface for the whole session
' whether or not a browser joins it.
'
' They are greyed but keep their TRUE state: a ticked greyed box reads as
' compulsory, which is what it is, and the help line says "always on" rather
' than "off" for one.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O5): "greyed" no longer names one look. An Off
' answer in force (a fact, or a compulsory box) draws FIXED, in plain ink. An
' Off answer not in force draws GATED, faint and struck through. Grey now
' means OFFERED: an answer the operator can pick and has not. The logic in
' this file is unchanged; read "greyed" below as "Off". The full style table:
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (ONE CARD, STATE STYLES).
'
' Naming the ALTERNATIVE is half of what a help line is for, and the half that
' was missing. An unticked box is a posture too, and "docker (sandbox)" said
' nothing about what unticking it selects — not the host, which proveo never
' runs an agent on, but (until 2026-10-16) the docker backend behind egress
' sidecars. Since that backend's deletion the box's help reads "Mount the
' current git project in a sandbox for the agent" (MEASURED, gateAddons).
'
' THE HELP PROMISES A DAEMON ONLY WHERE THE MANIFEST DOES (N20, DONE (wt)
' 2026-10-17). The form passes addonHelpFor(man) (internal/run/choices.go:60,
' :512-518): a clone of addonHelp — the shared map is never edited — whose
' sandbox line, for a `daemon: false` harness (hermes), reads "a microVM (sbx)
' with no Docker daemon for the agent — the boundary every run on this harness
' gets" instead of "a microVM with its own Docker daemon (sbx) — …". The option
' value stays "docker (sandbox)"; the column paints "sandbox".
' TestThePickerPromisesADaemonOnlyWhereTheManifestDoes
' (run_test.go:867) pins both texts and the untouched shared map.
'
' HISTORY: the egress axis was chosen by AVAILABILITY, not by the add-on.
' Consulting the remembered answer once offered the docker tiers —
' open/allowlist/review — for a run going to sbx, hiding changeBaselineHint.
' The tiers are deleted now; egressRow always shows sbx's baseline, locked.
'
' Help is what an option DOES, keyed by the option itself rather than indexed:
' callers assemble Options conditionally — a harness without a -browser variant
' is never offered one — and a parallel slice would then describe the wrong box.
'
' It exists because the picker could only ever explain what it had taken AWAY.
' Reason is written when something is gated off, so the two add-ons that were
' available and ticked carried no text, and the operator was left to
' infer "browser" and "docker (sandbox)" from their names.
'
' The block is drawn BELOW the row, never appended to it: the row is already ~70
' columns of checkboxes, so text after them runs off the terminal — which is how
' the one description the picker did have, a gated option's reason, came to end
' mid-sentence. It is WRAPPED rather than clipped, because these are sentences
' the operator is meant to read; the row's own Reason stays clipped, being a
' glance signal for a row the cursor is not on, with the full words below.
'
' ── RADIO VERSUS CHECKBOX IS A STATEMENT ABOUT REACHABLE STATES ────────────
' Brackets say "any number of these"; parentheses say "one of these". The
' execution plane is one of these, since a run has exactly one place it runs.
' Storage stays a checkbox set because "neither" is REACHABLE there. Execution
' keeps the checkbox model for a weaker reason now: retiring the privileged
' sidecar (_spec/_paradigms/retire-dind.puml) left it with one box, greyed and
' ticked, so it states a fact rather than offering a choice — and a radio of one
' would read as a question. Divider is declared rather than inferred: it used to be "the first
' multi-select row", which silently meant only one group could ever be named.
'
' ── WHERE THE CURSOR MAY REST ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' A single-select row's Selected IS the choice, so it may never rest on a gated
' option. On a MULTI row it is only the cursor — the checkbox is the choice, and
' toggle refuses a gated one on its own — so the cursor may stop there. That is
' what makes a greyed box's explanation readable: it is the one whose reason the
' operator most needs, and it was the one option the cursor could never reach.
'
' ── A LOCKED ROW IS HOVERABLE, AND Hover IS WHY ────────────────────────────
' A locked row reports a fact the operator cannot change, and its OPTIONS are
' the only statement of what that fact implies — what allow-all admits that
' deny-all does not. The cursor used to skip the row entirely, so those
' sentences existed and could not be read.
'
' Hover is a separate index from Selected, and the separation is the whole
' mechanism: on a locked row Selected is a FACT being shown, so moving it would
' rewrite the answer while pretending to explain it. The arrows move Hover,
' nothing reports as changed, and Selection() returns the baseline untouched.
'
' `move` admits a locked row; `firstSelectable` still does not. The first thing
' the operator meets should be something they can answer. The run form says
' where that is instead of deriving it: StartRow/StartOption open the cursor
' on the devices row, on browser — the first option the operator can
' actually change — because credentials has joined egress among the locked
' facts above it, hoverable to read and never to rewrite.
' DECIDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O8): REVERSED. The run form no longer names its
' start row; choiceui derives it for every form whose caller leaves StartRow
' empty. The cursor opens on the TOP row with an answer to change: not
' Locked, and a Field or at least one option that is not Off. On that row it
' opens on the current answer: a radio's Selected, a multi row's first
' changeable cell. With no such row it falls back to the top unlocked row,
' then row 0. Home goes to the same row. Init forms that name a StartRow keep
' it. The reason above still holds; the rows moved under it.
' [Inference] With the questions in order (owner, O7), a fixed
' StartRow=devices would skip every question above it. The owner stated the
' rule, not a reason.
' MEASURED (run_form_order_test.go, review step 9): claudecode, hermes and
' codex with no key and no login open on model (API keys, or plan on codex);
' cursor, with credentials locked, every OS option Off and no model row,
' opens on trust repo · off. The design suggested devices there; the
' Executor followed O8 as written.
' Form.StartsOn() reports the start row without moving the cursor, so
' internal/run can test it. firstChoice and StartOption left the run form.
'
' The UNDERLINE is the cursor mark and must survive the unavailable style, so it
' is applied after it — which also fixes an off option the cursor legitimately
' rests on in a MULTI row, where the warn style used to erase it.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O5): a FILL replaces the underline on option
' cells and open-list entries: black on brand, or black on grey when the
' cursor rests on a fixed or unavailable answer (struck through too when
' unavailable). answerStyle still tests the cursor first, so the mark still
' survives the unavailable style. A text field keeps its underline.
'
' ── THE REASON HAS ONE HOME, AND IT IS THE HELP BLOCK ──────────────────────
' It is no longer drawn on the row. Inline it trailed the options clipped
' to whatever width was left, which is how the locked sbx egress row's runnable
' command — the one statement of how to change a host-wide baseline — came to
' exist nowhere in full.
'
' The block wraps instead of clipping, and the cursor can now reach every row
' that has a reason, locked ones included. A locked row always states its
' reason there; any other row shows the hovered option's OffWhy, falling back to
' the row's reason when that option had nothing of its own to say — so hovering
' never shows LESS than the inline copy did.
'
' Three things fell out. ""anyOff"" lost its only caller and is gone. The width
' budget no longer reserves for the reason. The row name is clipped to its
' 16 columns, so ""rightEdge"" starts at the options, and the pane's breakpoint stops depending on how
' long a sentence is. And the pane can no longer clip a fact, because there is
' no fact on the row to clip — which retires the constraint that shaped it.
'
' ON A SCREEN TOO SMALL TO DRAW THE FORM, ONLY LEAVING IS ALLOWED. This prompt
' exists to confirm a credential and network posture, and silently CHANGING a
' posture nobody can see is worse than the truncation the viewport replaced —
' accepting one unseen is bad enough, and esc is always the answer to that.
'
' ── A HELP LINE HAS A PREFIX ONLY WHEN IT HAS A REASON ─────────────────────
' "off: " on its own is still a field, and an option that is merely AVAILABLE
' was printing that bare prefix under itself — a label announcing nothing. An
' available option says what it DOES and stops there; the prefix belongs to the
' explanation, so with no explanation there is no prefix and no line.
'
' ── THE HEADER'S ACCENT IS A VOCABULARY, NOT AN EMPHASIS ───────────────────
' putHeader styles a header row by what each piece IS, never by where it sits:
' MARKERS take the accent and CONTENT stays body-styled, so the eye can find
' the row's structure without reading it. The label, every `key=` in a
' multi-slot row, and every glyph are markers; model ids, tool names and
' provider names are content. A parenthetical state is a third thing — a
' description of the fact rather than the fact — and takes the aside style.
'
' The rule arrived from two rows that broke it in opposite directions.
' `llms:` accented only up to the label, so every slot after it rendered as
' body text and the row read as one model mattering more than the others — the
' same half-highlighted failure the wireframe records. `lsp:` (removed
' 2026-10-30) had the inverse risk: its glyphs and its server names sat in one
' string, and accenting the names would make the content compete with the
' markers meant to index it.
' `git: <repo> on <branch> (<state>)` is what pins the aside: a reader scans
' that row for the BRANCH.
'
' ── THE PAINT ORDER THE REGIONS DEPEND ON ──────────────────────────────────
' Topology is called at PAINT time on every frame, so it tracks the cursor —
' which `move` deliberately does not report through OnChange. It must be pure:
' it reads rows and never mutates the form it is handed, and a nil Topology
' means no strip, which is what every caller that does not want one gets free.
'
' The foot's count rides on the hint rather than taking a body line of its own:
' the rows are the scarce thing, and a region that exists to say the rows ran
' out must not be the reason one more of them did. The hint is clipped BEFORE
' the count is appended, so the count is not the first thing a narrow terminal
' cuts — on exactly the terminals where scrolling happens.
'
' The help block is drawn at y+2, not y+1: the hint sits at y and the block has
' always opened with a blank line under it. Under its own row the block shoved
' every row beneath it as the cursor moved; unreserved down here it shoved the
' figure instead, which is why the slot is reserved at its MAXIMUM height.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (Executor, E8): the card's bottom border takes that
' blank. The key line sits at y, ╰─╯ at y+1 and the help at y+2.
'
' drawTopology paints through its own pen rather than the canvas, so it has no
' window to be dropped by. The budget already guarantees the room; the guard is
' the belt to that pair of braces, because the one region outside the canvas is
' the one that could overrun it unnoticed. The pane is likewise anchored to the
' body's TOP line rather than centred: everything else here is top-anchored, and
' a centred figure would move whenever the body's height changed — re-breaking
' the thing the reserved help slot exists to hold still.
'
' headingsInWindow is the set of rows whose divider heading is on screen. Only
' those rows drop their own label only when the heading is that label. A
' declared Heading keeps the name: OS under execution, devices under
' interface. Every other row keeps its label, because its
' label is the only place its name was ever going to appear. Built once per
' frame rather than rescanned per line: the body repaints at the figure's rate.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13: the run form's four sections all declare a Heading
' (agent, execution, reach, interface), so credentials, OS, egress and
' devices all keep their labels. The heading is now a stub
' (wireframe.puml, ONE CARD). E7 expected this map to become unreachable; a
' row other than the cursor's still reaches it, so it stays (Executor).
'
' minHeight takes the WIDTH because the help slot's height depends on it. Asking
' at width zero measured the help wrapped to wrap()'s 20-column floor and
' reported a number far larger than the one layout actually tested — in the one
' region whose entire job is naming the right size.
title Choice prompt render — one card, four sections, the cursor on the first answer to change

node "internal/choiceui" as PKG <<host>> {
  component "Form\nBanner · Title · Header · Rows" as FORM <<app>>
  component "Row\nradio: Options + Selected\ncheckbox: Multi + On/Off" as ROW <<app>>
  component "draw(screen, cursor)\ncard · stubs · markers" as DRAW <<app>>
  component "Run()\na Bubble Tea model, one key per action" as RUN <<app>>
  component "OnChange(*Form)\nre-gated after every keystroke" as CHANGE <<app>>
  component "Selection · Selections\nread back by label" as READ <<app>>
}

node "cmd/proveo — what may be offered" as GATES <<host>> {
  component "applicableRows\ndrop an axis with nothing to decide" as APPL <<app>>
  component "comingSoon\ngrey out + move the selection off" as SOON <<app>>
  component "gateAddons · gateEvidence\ncross-row exclusivity" as GATE <<app>>
}

component "Operator terminal\nrequires a TTY" as TTY <<host>>
component "EnvHeader\ndetected secrets · settings" as HDR <<app>>
component "A locked or absent row read as an answer" as MISREAD <<error>>

GATES ARROW_MAIN FORM : rows built, then filtered
HDR ARROW_MAIN FORM
FORM ARROW_MAIN ROW
FORM ARROW_MAIN DRAW
RUN ARROW_MAIN DRAW : redraw per event
RUN ARROW_MAIN CHANGE
CHANGE ARROW_MAIN GATE
APPL ARROW_MAIN FORM
SOON ARROW_MAIN ROW
DRAW ARROW_MAIN TTY
TTY ARROW_MAIN RUN : Enter confirms · Esc/q cancels
RUN ARROW_MAIN READ
READ ARROW_ERROR MISREAD : fall back to the resolved value instead

' ── "agent evidence" BECAME "outputs" (2026-10-13) ─────────────────────────
' The row reads `outputs  ( ) filtered  (•) verbose`. Only the words changed:
' "filtered" is the old "default" level, and evidenceOf maps the answer back,
' so PROVEO_AGENT_EVIDENCE, the choice cache and agent_evidence_verbose keep
' "default"/"verbose". The ask was `[ ] filtered  [ ] verbose` checkboxes; the
' row stays RADIO because the level is one answer — two boxes would add a
' "neither" and a "both" the env var cannot carry
' (TestEvidenceIsOneAnswerNotTwoBoxes). The run-log key in internal/posture
' still says "agent evidence"; it is the log's vocabulary, not the prompt's.

note bottom of DRAW
  **""outputs"" is a toggle, not a tier.**
  Narrating more of the run costs tokens and
  screen rather than safety, so it sits under
  interface, not with the risk-ordered rows —
  as a RADIO row: a level is exactly one answer.
end note

note bottom of DRAW
  **Order is a property of the row, not of a
  legend.** Radio rows still run riskier to
  safer while a checkbox set has no direction,
  and since 2026-11-13 no caption claims either.
end note

note bottom of HDR
  **Hidden settings are not even named.** The
  header line that listed CODE_THEME and
  DARK_MODE is gone, while a model setting still
  prints NAME=value at the facts column.
end note

note left of FORM
  **No form claims a risk order.** The owner
  removed ""◀ riskier … safer ▶"" from every form
  on 2026-11-13, so ""NoAxis"" went with it while
  the columns kept their order.
end note

note top of GATE
  **One gate per toggle row, run
  unconditionally.** ""gateAddons"" degrades to a
  no-op when its row was filtered out, so both
  gates fire on every keystroke and the caller
  never tracks which rows survived onto the form.
end note

note top of GATE
  **A level is one answer, so it is a radio.**
  The gate that kept two checkboxes exclusive is
  gone: it left 'neither ticked' reachable, a
  state that quietly meant default and that the
  picker had no way to explain.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **An Off box means one of two opposite
  things.** Unavailable is unticked and drawn
  struck; compulsory is ticked and drawn fixed,
  which is execution's sandbox — and only the
  second is read back as a selected add-on.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **Off and ticked, outside ""addonFixed"".**
  The gate sets the sandbox Off on every run,
  and an unready sbx no longer unticks it,
  because since 2026-10-16 the run refuses
  before the form.
end note

note bottom of READ
  **""Selections"" drops every Off box, so the
  compulsory one is re-added deliberately.**
  Reporting the sandbox as unselected once
  routed the run to the docker backend; that
  backend is deleted, the re-add stays.
end note

note top of SOON
  **Shown, never hidden.** ""comingSoon""
  disables the option and moves the selection
  away, yet the row still draws it, struck, with
  the reason attached, because removing it
  misrepresents a withheld option as absent.
end note

note bottom of SOON
  **The flag accepts what the form greys.**
  ""--credentials forward"" works from the CLI
  while the form gates it. ""--egress-mode"" is
  an unknown flag since 2026-10-17.
end note

note top of TTY
  **""isStdinTTY"" gates every interactive
  prompt.** It performs a genuine ioctl check
  rather than a character-device stat, because
  ""/dev/null"" is itself a character device and
  would block a run that can never reply.
end note

note bottom of TTY
  **The add-ons picker runs BEFORE the
  missing-env wizard.** The wizard may attach a
  ""bufio\.Reader"" to stdin, and a buffered
  reader starves the picker of the keystrokes it
  is waiting for, hanging the prompt entirely.
end note

note top of HDR
  **Models are shown, not chosen.** The grid
  holds closed choices while a model id is an
  unbounded value, so the roles are printed in
  the header beside the repository instead of
  becoming a selectable row of their own.
end note

note bottom of HDR
  **Markers accent, content does not.** The
  label, each ""key="" and each glyph index the
  row; model ids, server names and providers are
  what the row says. A ""(state)"" aside is a
  description of the fact, so it is italic.
end note

note bottom of HDR
  **Each role carries the provider it resolved
  to.** That is what exposes a credential-less
  role BEFORE launch, rather than after an
  authentication failure on its first outbound
  call.
end note

note bottom of ROW
  Rows sit under named stubs: agent,
  execution, reach and interface.
end note

note bottom of RUN
  **The cursor opens on the first question.**
  It rests on the top row with an answer to
  change, on that row's current answer, unless
  the form names a StartRow of its own.
end note

note bottom of ROW
  **The consent modal is deleted.** ""review""
  answered one connection at a time over a
  suspended agent TUI; it was retired 2026-10-16
  and ""Consent"" went with it.
end note


@enduml
